<title>CHINA: Small earthquake rocks remote west China province.</title>
<headline>Small earthquake rocks remote west China province.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>An earthquake measuring 5.4 on the Richter scale has jolted a sparsely-populated area in China's western Qinghai province, the Xinhua news agency said on Monday.</p>
<p>No casualties were reported from the tremor, which struck at 7.28 p.m. on Sunday (1128 GMT), Xinhua said.</p>
<p>It gave no further details.</p>
</text>
